{% if include_claude_hooks -%}
- **`python3`** — runs the destructive-command guard's matcher
  ([`block-destructive.sh`](../.agents/hooks/block-destructive.sh)) and is the
  fallback reader for hook payloads. The guard *requires* it: with `python3`
  missing or unable to run, every Bash call is denied (fail closed) until one
  is installed. Usually preinstalled; otherwise `apt-get install python3` /
  `xcode-select --install` (macOS).
- **`jq`** (optional) — preferred reader for the Claude Code hook payloads in
  `.claude/settings.json` ([`hook-input.sh`](../.agents/hooks/hook-input.sh)
  falls back to `python3` when `jq` is missing *or cannot run*).
  Install: `apt-get install jq` / `brew install jq`.
